
# Rust build artifacts (Cargo.lock IS committed — the workspace ships binaries)
/target/
# The golden blocks (ABI §13.2) are their own cargo workspace, built on demand by
# `eio_conformance::golden`, so their artifacts are not under the workspace target dir.
# Their Cargo.lock IS committed: they are conformance fixtures, and a fixture that builds
# differently on two days is a fixture nobody can vouch for.
examples/blocks/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Release tarballs, from `just release-daemon` (SCOPE §7.2)
/dist/

# Designer (SvelteKit) artifacts
designer/node_modules/
designer/.svelte-kit/
designer/build/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Implementation plan files (transient artifacts of the /implement skill)
*.eio-plan.md

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
